  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-3812",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{p}^{2}}{2} & =4 \\\\ -{p}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {p}^{2} & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\np=\\pm \\sqrt{-8}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\\pm \\sqrt{-8} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{8\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
